(GW -- GD[Google Drive OAuth + Drive files]) Tj
T* (GW -- SMTP[SMTP mail.irpa.or.tz]) Tj
T* (GW -- WP[WordPress staging content API]) Tj
T* (GW -- CP[cPanel API / file operations]) Tj
T* (GW -- SOC[Social provider OAuth APIs]) Tj
T* (GW -- LK[LiveKit meeting media]) Tj
T* (GW -- KV[Cloudflare KV]) Tj
T* (GW -- DO[Cloudflare Durable Object: ESIGN_DO]) Tj
T* (FE -- FN[Firebase Functions]) Tj
T* (GC[Separate grant crawler Worker] -- D1[Isolated Cloudflare D1]) Tj
T* (IMPLEMENTED architecture observations) Tj
T* (- Frontend uses React 19, Vite and Firebase JS SDK 11; app navigation and role projection are primarily in src/App.jsx .) Tj
T* (- Firebase config initializes Auth and Firestore with persistent local cache and multi-tab manager. Applicant enrollment has a separate named Firebase app instance.) Tj
T* (- The frontend Worker serves built assets from dist ; Firebase Hosting rewrites SPA routes to index.html .) Tj
T* (- Drive Gateway uses Cloudflare Worker entry drive-gateway/src/index.js , router modules and Firestore REST/admin token logic. It is configured with Google Drive, SMTP, KV and e-signature Durable Object bindings.) Tj
T* (- A separate grant crawler exists; its parallel implementation stores discovered public-call metadata in isolated D1 and explicitly does not yet synchronize to production Firestore.) Tj
T* (- Browser permission projection is not a security boundary; Firestore rules and trusted backend checks remain authoritative.) Tj
T* (GAP: no single authoritative architecture diagram or complete runtime deployment inventory was found that proves all environments and bindings are currently active.) Tj
T* (2.2 Product functions) Tj
T* (The product functions are captured by the functional requirements in  3 and page inventory in  6. The current NAV constant declares 31 top-level modules , not 26. The source separately declares 15 nested sub-portals . The application also has standalone authentication, invitation activation, entry gateway, signature and modal states.) Tj
T* (2.3 User classes and roles) Tj
T* (Source-visible role families include Administrator; Executive Director; Board Chairperson, Vice Chairperson, Secretary, Treasurer and Board Member; department directors; Internal Oversight roles; HR Manager/Officer; Finance Manager/Officer/Accountant/Finance Personnel; Procurement Officer/Manager/Team Member; Programme/Technical Officer; Operations Manager; IT Specialist/Information Technology Officer; Communications Officer/Manager, Media Officer, Public Relations Officer and Approver; External Auditor; special invitees, observers and view-only recipients; and induction applicants.) Tj
T* (Role membership and effective access are resolved from active member/employee/auditor/admin profiles and permission policy. Departmental module mapping is also present. The complete live roster and assignment matrix is data-dependent and cannot be enumerated from source alone.) Tj
T* (2.4 Operating environment) Tj
T* (- Web: modern browser with JavaScript, HTTPS, Firebase Auth and network access.) Tj
T* (- Mobile: responsive web/PWA at 390 CSS px target width; manifest display mode standalone.) Tj
T* (- Windows: Electron BrowserWindow; context isolation on, Node integration off, sandbox on; HTTPS URL with offline HTML fallback.) Tj
T* (- Android: Capacitor; local dist webDir; no remote server.url to preserve local/offline startup.) Tj
T* (- Server: Cloudflare Workers, Firebase Auth/Firestore/Functions, Google Drive, SMTP, WordPress and cPanel APIs; LiveKit for meeting media.) Tj
T* (- Build/test: Node.js/npm, Vite, Firebase emulator/rules test tooling, Playwright/browser tests and GitHub Actions workflows.) Tj
T* (2.5 Design and implementation constraints) Tj
T* (1. Cloudflare-first gateway: document references, controlled document lifecycle, signing, invitation mail and multiple governance services use Cloudflare routes. Do not add a Firebase Function/client fallback where source explicitly fails closed.) Tj
T* (2. Firebase plan and quotas: Firestore/Auth/Functions limits and pricing are external operational constraints. PROPOSED: document quota budgets, alert thresholds and capacity tests before production scale.) Tj
T* (3. Offline: service worker caches a limited static shell and excludes API/auth/signature/invitation/token/upload/approval/PDF traffic. Offline mode is not an offline governance transaction engine.) Tj
T* (4. Security: client-side navigation/permission projection is not authoritative; server and Firestore rules govern data.) Tj
T* (5. Environment isolation: Actual-only identity/security records must not be routed into Trial data. Gateway staging and production are separate configurations.) Tj
T* (6. No production mutation in this task: all work is documentation-only.) Tj
T* (7. Integration credentials: secrets are environment-managed; they must never be printed, stored in source or returned by diagnostics.) Tj
T* (2.6 Assumptions and dependencies) Tj
T* (- Firebase project IDs, Cloudflare bindings, OAuth credentials, Google Drive permissions, SMTP mailbox and third-party accounts are provisioned by IRPA operators.) Tj
T* (- Network-dependent functions require network availability; static shell/offline fallback is the only evidenced offline guarantee.) Tj
T* (- A valid, active institutional register record is required for protected identity and signing operations.) Tj
T* (- WordPress editing is intentionally restricted to a dedicated staging WordPress host/account in the code-level website editor; cPanel production/staging roots are environment-restricted.) Tj
T* (- GAP: no verified SLA, RPO/RTO, retention schedule, accessibility conformance statement or user-volume forecast was found.) Tj
T* (3. Functional requirements) Tj
T* (Priority meanings: P1 = governance/security critical; P2 = important operational capability; P3 = supporting capability. Acceptance criteria are testable statements derived from source behaviour; where the code only partially implements the stated user goal, that limitation is recorded in  9.) Tj
T* (Requirement ID Requirement Priority Acceptance criteria Portal / page) Tj
T* (--- --- --- --- ---) Tj
ET
endstream
