(GEN-FR-001 Authenticate users using the configured Firebase Authentication providers and preserve the authenticated session. P1 Login accepts a valid credential and rejects invalid or expired credentials; protected screens are not exposed to signed-out users. Authentication / Dashboard) Tj
T* (GEN-FR-002 Resolve the user's active institutional identity and role context from the member, employee, auditor or administrator registers. P1 A test identity resolves to its active authoritative profile; inactive or unlinked identities are denied protected access. Dashboard / Members & Personnel) Tj
T* (GEN-FR-003 Display role-appropriate navigation and apply trusted Firestore/Worker authorization independently of client-side visibility. P1 Direct requests to restricted records and endpoints are rejected even if a user manually opens a hidden screen. All portals) Tj
T* (GEN-FR-004 Provide the shared application shell, global navigation, in-portal navigation and page Back/Next navigation. P1 Navigation changes the selected module without exposing registered child portals as unrelated top-level items. Shared shell) Tj
T* (GEN-FR-005 Require an explicit selection of Trial or Actual data environment before protected portal use; keep identity/security records in Actual. P1 Trial records are marked and isolated; actual access requires confirmation and the configured server-side gate. Data Environment Gate) Tj
T* (INV-FR-001 Allow an authorised operator to create and manage member/employee invitations linked to an institutional record. P1 Invitation stores recipient, role and canonical record linkage; duplicate/mismatched records are rejected. Invitations) Tj
T* (INV-FR-002 Send invitation messages through the configured gateway mail service and record delivery outcome. P1 A valid request returns a safe status; mail failure is visible without exposing credentials. Invitations / SMTP) Tj
T* (INV-FR-003 Redeem an invitation token only for the matching authenticated email and valid invitation state. P1 Expired, cancelled, mismatched or already-claimed tokens are rejected with safe errors. Invitation Activation) Tj
T* (INV-FR-004 Allow the invitee to create or configure a password and complete account activation. P1 Successful activation links the Firebase UID to the authoritative member/employee record and marks invitation Activated. Invitation Activation) Tj
T* (INV-FR-005 Support induction and registration records before institutional account activation. P2 An induction application is stored and lookup returns only the matching authorised application. Induction and Orientation) Tj
T* (MEM-FR-001 Maintain Board Member, Member and Employee institutional registers with unique references and status. P1 Create/update actions validate required identity fields and preserve canonical records without duplicate account records. Board Members Registration / Members & Personnel) Tj
T* (MEM-FR-002 Associate one Firebase identity with both member and employee records where the person holds both capacities. P1 Activation updates the linked records with the same UID and does not create a duplicate governance record. Members & Personnel) Tj
T* (MEET-FR-001 Create, update and delete meeting register entries subject to role and lifecycle policy. P1 Only authorised actors can perform each operation; invalid transitions return an explicit error. Meetings) Tj
T* (MEET-FR-002 Issue, update and revoke meeting access invitations and authorise entry against meeting-specific policy. P1 A non-participant cannot enter a protected meeting room; revoked access is rejected. Meeting Entry Gateway / Participants) Tj
T* (MEET-FR-003 Provide meeting room participation, activity and subscription views scoped to the current user and meeting. P1 A participant sees only authorised meeting activity and subscriptions. Meeting Room / Participants) Tj
T* (MEET-FR-004 Capture meeting records, proceedings, drafts, transcripts and translation outputs through gateway services. P2 Record retrieval enforces meeting scope and retention/legal-hold protection. Meeting Room) Tj
T* (MEET-FR-005 Support meeting voting open/close, resolution, decision and action records. P1 Voting cannot be cast outside the open window or by an unauthorised actor; decision links are preserved. Voting / Resolutions / Decisions / Actions) Tj
T* (MEET-FR-006 Support meeting media tokens and recording start/stop/status through configured LiveKit credentials. P2 Missing LiveKit configuration returns a controlled service-unavailable response; media credentials are not exposed. Meeting Room) Tj
T* (DOC-FR-001 Issue a unique controlled-document reference through the Cloudflare service. P1 Reference issuance requires authentication and fails closed when the gateway is unavailable. Documents) Tj
T* (DOC-FR-002 Upload controlled documents with type, classification, archive category, version and record-origin metadata. P1 Invalid file type/size or failed policy check blocks upload and does not create a misleading completed record. Upload Document) Tj
T* (DOC-FR-003 List, retrieve, download and share documents according to document-level access policy. P1 Unauthorised users cannot list or download protected document content. My Documents / Department Documents / Shared With Me) Tj
T* (DOC-FR-004 Apply document lifecycle transitions and retain lifecycle history. P1 Only permitted transitions succeed; each transition records actor/time and rejects invalid state changes. Documents / Post-Signature Work) Tj
T* (DOC-FR-005 Provision and retrieve department, signature and final archive locations in Google Drive. P1 Archive operations return verified references; failed archive writes are visible and retryable without duplicate completion. Final Archive / Retrieve Archived Documents) Tj
T* (SIG-FR-001 Create a signature workflow/envelope and define ordered or optional signers and access-only recipients. P1 Recipients are validated and view-only recipients are not treated as action signers. Signature Platform / Signing Workspace) Tj
T* (SIG-FR-002 Verify signer identity and authority against active member/employee registers before signature execution. P1 Manual authority text that does not match an active register entry is rejected. Signature Platform) Tj
T* (SIG-FR-003 Capture signature input through the signature pad and bind signature fields to the document. P1 The signer confirms the intended signature action; field geometry and signer identity are retained. Signature Platform / Signature pad) Tj
T* (SIG-FR-004 Submit and complete signing through the gateway, preserving evidence and document hash. P1 Completion is atomic or remains visibly pending; hash/evidence and signer status can be retrieved. Signature Platform) Tj
T* (SIG-FR-005 Mirror completed signature state to Firestore and archive signed documents in Drive. P1 A failed mirror/archive does not display false completion; reconciliation and retry status are available. Post-Signature Work / Final Archive) Tj
T* (SIG-FR-006 Support signer invitation, decline, void, status, evidence and completion retry operations. P1 Each action validates the token/actor and records its resulting state. Signature Platform) Tj
T* (AUTH-FR-001 Create authorization requests with requester, reviewer, approver, implementer, basis, justification and linked evidence. P1 Required fields and named reviewer/approver are enforced; requester cannot self-approve. Authorization & Approvals) Tj
T* (AUTH-FR-002 Enforce the Draft   Submitted   Under Review   Approved/Rejected/Returned   Completed state machine. P1 Only the designated actor and permitted transition can change state; reasons are required for return/rejection/approval. Authorization & Approvals) Tj
T* (AUTH-FR-003 Record decision basis, conditions, authority confirmation, history and audit events. P1 Every transition writes immutable history and an associated audit event. Authorization & Approvals / Audit Trail) Tj
T* (FIN-FR-001 Maintain finance budgets, transactions, funding, approvals, commitments, grants, accounts, reconciliations, assets, journals and reports. P1 Finance operations validate required values, role permissions and audit events; no unsupported accounting policy is assumed. Finance Portfolio) Tj
T* (FIN-FR-002 Maintain staff payment requests and payment trace references. P2 A trace has creator/updater identity and timestamp; finance access is enforced. Employee Payments / Finance Portfolio) Tj
T* (PROC-FR-001 Maintain procurement requests, vendors, scores, blacklist and probation status. P1 Vendor and procurement actions are permission-gated and auditable. Procurement) Tj
T* (RISK-FR-001 Maintain risk register entries, reports, decisions and actions as governance evidence. P2 Restricted records are not exposed to unauthorised departmental users. Risk Register / Reports) Tj
T* (RES-FR-001 Provide research studies, datasets, observations, analyses, knowledge, outputs, instruments and submissions. P2 Dataset records preserve metadata and authorised access; release readiness remains separately controlled. Research, Statistics and Knowledge) Tj
T* (RES-FR-002 Support information requests, information grants, shared information, updates, tool permissions and portal alerts. P2 A request/update is visible only to permitted roles and is traceable. Research portal) Tj
T* (GRANT-FR-001 Discover public grant opportunities through crawler sources and persist opportunity metadata in its configured store. P2 Crawler run records report source health and discovery outcomes; no application submission is inferred. Grant Intelligence) Tj
T* (GRANT-FR-002 Support grant source registry, relevance screening and funding pipeline records. P2 Each source/opportunity retains provenance and status; external application submission is not assumed. Grant Intelligence) Tj
T* (COM-FR-001 Create and edit communications editorial items and website page/post drafts. P2 Only authorised authors can create/edit; revisions increment and status returns to Draft after edit. Communication & Media) Tj
T* (COM-FR-002 Submit editorial content for approval and enforce separation of author and approver. P1 Author cannot approve own content; only pending items can be approved/rejected. Communication & Media) Tj
T* (COM-FR-003 Connect to WordPress staging for content status, list, read and controlled update operations. P2 Production WordPress host is rejected by the staging editor; missing configuration returns safe 503. Website Studio) Tj
T* (COM-FR-004 Connect social accounts and use platform-specific OAuth/publishing routes where configured. P2 No publish is represented as successful unless provider response confirms it; global pause is respected. Social Media / Communication & Media) Tj
T* (COM-FR-005 Maintain communication/media asset metadata including URL, caption, credit and consent status. P2 Only HTTPS asset URLs are accepted; consent status is explicit and metadata save is distinct from asset upload. Media Library) Tj
T* (SYS-FR-001 Expose administrator system diagnostics and release-readiness checks without returning secret values. P1 Only authorised administrators can run checks; output reports presence/status, never credential content. IT Operations / Release Readiness) Tj
T* (SYS-FR-002 Provide settings, administrator provisioning, department archive registry and department portal definitions. P2 Only designated roles can administer; portal definitions and department records are persisted and auditable. Settings / System) Tj
T* (SYS-FR-003 Provide downloadable application resources and release artefacts. P3 Only existing downloadable artefacts are listed; missing artefacts are clearly indicated. Downloads) Tj
ET
