(OFF-FR-001 Install as a PWA with a versioned service-worker shell and manifest. P1 Install metadata and shell assets load; API/auth/signature/upload traffic is excluded from cache. PWA) Tj
T* (OFF-FR-002 Provide an offline fallback for navigation shell startup and static assets. P1 When network is unavailable, cached shell or offline page appears; protected operations are not falsely reported as available. PWA / Offline) Tj
T* (OFF-FR-003 Package Windows desktop using Electron with context isolation, sandbox and no Node integration. P2 Desktop app loads configured HTTPS app and falls back to offline page on failed navigation. Windows desktop) Tj
T* (OFF-FR-004 Package Android with Capacitor and local dist web assets for offline startup. P2 Android config uses local webDir and does not force a remote server URL; offline startup is tested. Android) Tj
T* (REL-FR-001 Run automated unit, policy, integration and browser regression checks before release. P1 Release evidence records command, commit, result and any skipped test. Release Readiness) Tj
T* (REL-FR-002 Deploy frontend and gateway through separate controlled workflows with environment isolation. P1 Production deployment requires explicit approval and validated staging; this documentation change does not deploy. Release process) Tj
T* (REL-FR-003 Maintain documented rollback path for frontend, Worker and data migration changes. P1 Rollback identifies immutable release refs and data recovery limitations; no untested reverse migration is assumed. Release process) Tj
T* (4. External interface requirements) Tj
T* (4.1 User interfaces) Tj
T* (The shared shell includes branded header/identity area, global portal category navigation \(IT, Governance, Finance, Evidence, Funding, Communications, System\), in-portal parent/sub-portal roller, page Back/Next navigation with world-time panel, main content, responsive/mobile navigation and footer. The current shell also contains a data-environment gate and offline/install UI. Exact fixed/sticky positioning is a UI implementation detail; wireframes in wireframes/ are low-fidelity, not pixel-perfect.) Tj
T* (4.2 Software interfaces) Tj
T* (- Firebase Authentication: email/password, Google sign-in/redirect, magic link and invitation activation/password setup paths.) Tj
T* (- Firestore: institutional registers, meeting/governance, finance/procurement, research, grant and communications records; client uses persistent local cache. Firestore rules are authoritative.) Tj
T* (- Cloudflare Drive Gateway: REST routes in  4.4; Firebase ID token authentication and server-side Firestore admin access.) Tj
T* (- Google Drive: OAuth start/callback, folder provisioning, controlled document storage, archive and download.) Tj
T* (- SMTP: gateway mail delivery; configured host in Wrangler is mail.irpa.or.tz , port 465, sender info@irpa.or.tz \(configuration values, not credential proof\).) Tj
T* (- WordPress: content/status integration via communicationsSite.mjs ; editor restricted to staging host and dedicated Editor account.) Tj
T* (- cPanel: account-level API/file operations constrained by environment and document root.) Tj
T* (- Social platforms: Meta, LinkedIn, X, YouTube and WhatsApp configuration hooks; actual connected status is not proven by source.) Tj
T* (- LiveKit: meeting media token/recording services; runtime requires LIVEKIT_URL/API key/secret.) Tj
T* (- Grant discovery: separate Cloudflare Worker and D1 database; parallel crawler is isolated and Firebase sync intentionally disabled.) Tj
T* (4.3 Communications integration configuration) Tj
T* (Code reads WordPress WORDPRESS_BASE_URL , WORDPRESS_USERNAME , WORDPRESS_APPLICATION_PASSWORD ; cPanel CPANEL_BASE_URL , CPANEL_USERNAME , CPANEL_API_TOKEN , CPANEL_DOCUMENT_ROOT ; and social-provider configuration variables. The diagnostics endpoint reports presence only. Do not expose or include secret values in documentation or logs. GAP: runtime binding status was not read during this documentation task.) Tj
T* (4.4 Gateway route inventory) Tj
T* (The following route groups are present in the inspected Worker dispatch and delegated routers. Braced alternatives denote route families; methods shown are registered methods, not proof of successful production operation.) Tj
