(--- --- ---) Tj
T* (NFR-SEC-001 Authentication Protected actions require valid Firebase identity; verify token expiry and invalid-token handling.) Tj
T* (NFR-SEC-002 Authorization Enforce least privilege at Firestore/Worker; direct API tests must deny unauthorised access even when UI is bypassed.) Tj
T* (NFR-SEC-003 Separation of duties Requester cannot approve own authorization; communications author cannot approve own item; signer role and authority are verified.) Tj
T* (NFR-SEC-004 Data isolation Trial and Actual records remain separated; Actual-only collections include identity/security registers, audit, signatures and settings.) Tj
T* (NFR-SEC-005 Secret handling No secrets in client bundle, source control, logs or diagnostic responses; verify redaction and secret presence checks.) Tj
T* (NFR-AUD-001 Auditability Governance and finance mutations record actor, action, record reference and timestamp; verify event correlation and failure handling.) Tj
T* (NFR-REL-001 Reliability Signature completion/mirroring and document archive operations must fail visibly and support controlled reconciliation/retry.) Tj
T* (NFR-PERF-001 Performance PROPOSED: define measurable page/API latency budgets and test at representative dataset sizes; no numeric SLO found.) Tj
T* (NFR-ACC-001 Accessibility PROPOSED: WCAG 2.2 AA target; keyboard navigation, focus visibility, labels, contrast, zoom and screen-reader checks.) Tj
T* (NFR-RESP-001 Responsive UI PROPOSED target: support 390 844 mobile and 1440 900 desktop without horizontal page overflow or control overlap.) Tj
T* (NFR-OFF-001 Offline Cache static shell only; do not cache authentication, signatures, uploads, approvals or API traffic. Display clear offline state.) Tj
T* (NFR-BCP-001 Backup/recovery GAP: no complete tested recovery plan, RPO/RTO, Firestore export schedule, Drive recovery procedure or key escrow runbook verified.) Tj
T* (NFR-MAINT-001 Maintainability Keep Worker route contracts, collection catalogue, page inventory and requirement traceability current with code changes.) Tj
T* (NFR-PRIV-001 Privacy Restrict member, employee, auditor, meeting, signature and finance records by need-to-know; avoid exposing private information in diagnostics.) Tj
T* (6. Data model) Tj
T* (6.1 Firestore collection inventory) Tj
T* (The COLLECTIONS registry in src/firebase/data.js explicitly names: members , employees , employeeCounters , memberCounters , participants , meetings , meetingSubscriptions , meetingRoomEvents , transcriptions , resolutions , votes , voteLocks , voteCorrections , votingIssues , actions , documents , documentTranslationRequests , signatures , decisions , risks , audit , reports , authorizationRequests , workflowActions , staffPaymentRequests , financeBudgets , financeTransactions , financeFunding , financeApprovals , financeCommitments , financeGrants , financeBankAccounts , financeReconciliations , financeAssets , financeRisks , financeReports , financeChartOfAccounts , financeJournalBatches , financePeriods , financeLedgerJournals , financeLedgerEntries , financePaymentMatches , financePaymentTrace , financeReferenceRegistry , procurementVendors , procurementRequests , procurementVendorScores , procurementVendorBlacklist , procurementVendorProbation , invitations , registrationRequests , inductionRecords , adminProfiles , auditorProfiles , systemSettings , mail , donorFunders , grantReportingObligations , researchStudies , researchDatasets , researchObservations , researchAnalyses , researchKnowledge , researchOutputs , researchInstruments , researchSubmissions , researchInformationRequests , researchInformationGrants , researchSharedInformation , researchUpdates , researchToolPermissions , researchPortalAlerts , institutionalDepartments , departmentArchives , signatureProfiles , signatureEnvelopes , signatureEvents , socialMediaAccounts , socialMediaAccountsAudit , communicationMediaItems , portalDefinitions . Additional source references include signatureProfiles , signatureEnvelopes , signatureEvents , socialMediaAccounts , socialMediaAccountsAudit , communicationMediaItems , and portalDefinitions . This is a source-discovered collection catalogue, not proof that every collection currently contains records.) Tj
T* (6.2 Key fields and relationships) Tj
T* (- members / employees: institutional person identity, role\(s\), email, status, registration/activation status, Firebase UID, invitation linkage, department/designation and registration number. A person may be linked to both registers with one UID; board/member register remains canonical for board identity.) Tj
T* (- invitations: recipient email/name, role/member type, institutional record type/id, member/employee/board-member linkage, status, accepted UID/time, activation flags and expiry/token metadata \(exact field set varies by workflow\).) Tj
T* (- meetings: meeting metadata, participants, access/subscription records, agenda/proceedings, meeting records, media/recording status and related decisions/resolutions/votes/actions.) Tj
T* (- documents: reference, title, type, archive category, classification, version, origin, Drive identifiers, lifecycle stage, parent-document and signature-envelope links.) Tj
T* (- signatureProfiles / signatureEnvelopes / signatures / signatureEvents: signer profile, envelope/document linkage, recipients/order, state, field coordinates, evidence, hashes and event history.) Tj
T* (- workflowActions / authorizationRequests / audit: request fields, participants \(UIDs\), status, stage index/version, decision record, history, related-document links and actor/time audit.) Tj
T* (- finance and procurement : finance-specific registers and ledger structures; source identifies named collections but a full canonical field schema is not consolidated in one schema file.) Tj
T* (- research : study/dataset/observation/analysis/knowledge/output/instrument/submission and information exchange records.) Tj
T* (- communications: editorial items/audit are stored in Cloudflare KV; media/social/website data also use Firestore or remote APIs as implemented.) Tj
T* (- grant opportunities: parallel discovery worker uses isolated D1 tables/migrations; not the same persistence boundary as the Firestore donor/funder and reporting-obligation collections.) Tj
