(7.1 Appointment   acceptance   registration   invitation   password   activation) Tj
T* (1. Administrator/authorised operator creates or identifies the institutional member/employee record.) Tj
T* (2. Invitation record links to the canonical institutional record and carries role/member type and recipient email.) Tj
T* (3. Gateway sends the invitation email through configured SMTP.) Tj
T* (4. Invitee opens the invitation link and authenticates using the invitation email.) Tj
T* (5. Gateway validates token/session state, expiry, cancellation and email binding.) Tj
T* (6. Invitee sets/configures password; activation links Firebase UID to member/employee record\(s\).) Tj
T* (7. Invitation status becomes Activated; protected navigation is resolved from active profiles.) Tj
T* (8. GAP: the complete human appointment/board resolution/acceptance process before the register entry is not fully evidenced as one end-to-end application workflow; document as external governance input until verified.) Tj
T* (7.2 Upload   signature   approval   archive) Tj
T* (1. User selects Trial/Actual environment and requests controlled document reference.) Tj
T* (2. User uploads with type/classification/version/archive metadata; gateway policy checks and registers document.) Tj
T* (3. Document is assigned to signature workflow; signer order, authority and signature fields are validated.) Tj
T* (4. Signers receive invitations and sign through authenticated signer UI/pad or controlled token flow.) Tj
T* (5. Gateway records signature evidence/hash and completion state; mirror into Firestore.) Tj
T* (6. Document lifecycle transitions to post-signature and final archive; Drive archive reference is recorded.) Tj
T* (7. Reconciliation/retry handles incomplete mirror/archive; completion is not shown until verified.) Tj
T* (8. Authorisation/approval workflows are distinct from e-signature and must be linked explicitly where required; signature alone does not equal institutional approval.) Tj
T* (7.3 Meetings) Tj
T* (1. Authorised user creates meeting register entry and participants.) Tj
T* (2. Meeting access invitation issued; gateway verifies identity, participant membership and meeting scope.) Tj
T* (3. Meeting Room supports activity, subscriptions, working documents, attendance, media/recording and proceedings where configured.) Tj
T* (4. Resolutions, votes, decisions and actions are recorded under meeting policy.) Tj
T* (5. Reports/transcripts may be compiled, translated and emailed.) Tj
T* (6. Retention/disposal is subject to protection/legal hold and server policy.) Tj
T* (7.4 Grant intelligence) Tj
T* (1. Discovery Worker polls public RSS/Atom and official donor sources \(parallel crawler also has optional Brave Search\).) Tj
T* (2. Candidates are normalized, deduplicated and screened for relevance, deadline, geography and eligibility.) Tj
T* (3. Parallel Worker writes metadata to isolated D1; production Firebase synchronization is intentionally disabled in that deployment.) Tj
T* (4. Frontend Grant Intelligence / source registry supports source/opportunity review.) Tj
T* (5. GAP: source discovery is not equivalent to a complete donor application drafting/submission workflow; no auto-submission is asserted.) Tj
T* (7.5 Communications and media) Tj
T* (1. Author creates editorial post or website-page draft with language, platform, link/image and optional schedule.) Tj
T* (2. Author submits; approver reviews and approves or returns/rejects; author cannot self-approve.) Tj
T* (3. Global publishing pause is administrator-controlled.) Tj
T* (4. WordPress Website Studio reads staging pages/posts and updates allowed fields only; cPanel integration handles website file operations under constrained root.) Tj
T* (5. Media Library stores metadata \(HTTPS asset URL, caption, credit, consent status\); asset upload is separate.) Tj
T* (6. Social account OAuth/status/publishing routes operate only when provider credentials and connection state are configured.) Tj
T* (7. GAP: provider-by-provider production publishing, webhook delivery and post-publication reconciliation were not live-tested.) Tj
T* (8. Verification, release and rollback) Tj
T* (8.1 Test strategy) Tj
T* (- Unit/policy tests: authorization, invitation, meeting categories, finance, communications, signature policy, document lifecycle.) Tj
T* (- Rules tests: Firestore security rules using emulator/rules-unit-testing.) Tj
T* (- Gateway tests: route contracts, authentication, upload lifecycle, Drive ID reconciliation, signature atomic completion, communications, release readiness.) Tj
T* (- Browser tests: authenticated governance regression, portal navigation, meeting portal, fundraising registry responsiveness.) Tj
T* (- PWA tests: service worker install/offline shell, excluded request classes.) Tj
T* (- Build tests: root Vite build; desktop package build; Android APK/release workflows.) Tj
T* (- Integration tests: staging only, isolated WordPress/cPanel and social/OAuth credentials; never run production mutations for routine verification.) Tj
ET
endstream
