(8.2 Release gates) Tj
T* (1. Code review and CI pass against immutable commit.) Tj
T* (2. Staging Worker/frontend build and integration tests pass with isolated staging resources.) Tj
T* (3. Firestore rules tests and authorization boundary tests pass.) Tj
T* (4. Signature lifecycle acceptance validates create   sign   mirror   archive, including failure/retry.) Tj
T* (5. PWA/Android/Windows package smoke tests pass.) Tj
T* (6. Release Readiness diagnostics show no unresolved critical failures and do not expose secrets.) Tj
T* (7. Explicit human production authorization; no implicit production deployment from documentation PR.) Tj
T* (8.3 Rollback) Tj
T* (- Frontend: redeploy the last known-good immutable build/commit through the approved workflow.) Tj
T* (- Worker: restore the previous Worker version/configuration via controlled deployment history; verify bindings and route health.) Tj
T* (- Firestore: restore from verified export/backup or perform a reviewed compensating correction; do not assume code rollback reverses data writes.) Tj
T* (- Google Drive: recover from retained versions/archives and reconcile Firestore references; do not delete evidence during rollback.) Tj
T* (- WordPress/cPanel: restore prior content/file backup using staging validation first.) Tj
T* (- Android/Windows: publish prior signed package and document version compatibility.) Tj
T* (- GAP: verified RPO/RTO, backup cadence, restore drill evidence and a named rollback owner were not located.) Tj
T* (9. Known gaps, defects and open decisions) Tj
T* (9.1 Confirmed source-level gaps / risks) Tj
T* (- GAP-001   Gateway disconnected in app shell: IRPA_GATEWAY_CONNECTED=false is explicitly set in src/App.jsx ; comments describe a temporary gateway disconnect.) Tj
T* (- GAP-002   Temporary data gate: IRPA_TEMPORARY_DATA_GATE_ENABLED=true ; operational implications and removal criteria are undocumented in the inspected source.) Tj
T* (- GAP-003   Live runtime unverified: deployed web app could not be inspected with an authenticated session; live role/menu, integration reachability, production data and responsive rendering remain unverified.) Tj
T* (- GAP-004   Page count discrepancy: requested baseline said 26 pages; source NAV currently contains 31 top-level modules and 15 nested sub-portals. IRPA must confirm whether 26 refers to an older or role-filtered menu.) Tj
T* (- GAP-005   Offline scope: service worker caches app shell/assets only and excludes auth, APIs, signature, invitation, upload, approval and PDFs. No offline transaction queue/sync is evidenced.) Tj
T* (- GAP-006   Collection schema: collection names are discoverable, but there is no single complete typed field schema and relationship contract for all 80+ collections.) Tj
T* (- GAP-007   Backup/DR: no end-to-end tested backup/restore, RPO/RTO or recovery evidence was established.) Tj
T* (- GAP-008   Performance/accessibility: no numeric latency SLO or WCAG conformance test report verified.) Tj
T* (- GAP-009   Grant crawler integration: parallel crawler D1 is isolated and Firebase sync is intentionally off; do not assume its discovered records automatically populate production Grant Intelligence.) Tj
T* (- GAP-010   Social/website integrations: WordPress/cPanel/social code paths exist, but live credentials, account permissions and actual production publishing state were not verified.) Tj
T* (- GAP-011   Android/Windows distribution: packaging workflows/configuration exist; current signed artifacts, distribution channel, support matrix and installed-version telemetry were not verified.) Tj
T* (- GAP-012   Approval vs signature: institutional approval workflow and e-signature workflow are separate; policy for mandatory ordering/linkage by document category needs IRPA decision.) Tj
T* (9.2 Decisions requiring IRPA input) Tj
T* (1. Is the approved scope 26 pages, or the 31 NAV modules + 15 sub-portals currently in source?) Tj
T* (2. What is the canonical role catalogue and who approves changes to role-to-portal and role-to-action permissions?) Tj
T* (3. Which workflow is authoritative for appointment/board acceptance before invitations are issued?) Tj
T* (4. Which document categories require approval, signature, both, or neither, and in what order?) Tj
T* (5. What are the approved retention periods, legal-hold triggers, disposal authorities and archive ownership?) Tj
T* (6. What offline actions, if any, may be drafted locally and synchronized later? Current code does not evidence offline writes for protected workflows.) Tj
T* (7. What backup frequency, RPO/RTO, recovery owner and annual restore test are required?) Tj
T* (8. Is WordPress editing strictly staging-only, and what is the separately approved production publishing process?) Tj
T* (9. Which social platforms are approved for live publishing and which roles may authorize posts?) Tj
T* (10. Should grant-crawler D1 results remain isolated, or is a reviewed least-privilege sync to Firestore required?) Tj
T* (11. What target browsers, Android versions, Windows versions and accessibility conformance level should be supported?) Tj
T* (12. What are numeric performance targets and expected concurrent user/data volumes?) Tj
T* (10. Traceability and page inventory) Tj
T* (10.1 Top-level portal/page inventory) Tj
T* (The source NAV contains 31 top-level modules.) Tj
T* (Page ID Page / module Navigation group Source) Tj
T* (--- --- --- ---) Tj
ET
